    "q-89354": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89354",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following random variables could be modeled as a binomial distribution?\n\n- The number of baskets made by a basketball player attempting three free throws if the probability of scoring any free throw is $65%$\n- The number of defective items in a random sample of $100$ items produced by a machine\n- The number of views of a video on a popular video channel",
      "worked_solution": "A binomial distribution models the number of successes in a sequence of $n$ independent experiments (where each outcome is either success or failure).\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of baskets in $3$ throws can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $3$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable II could be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of defective items in a random sample of $100$ items can be interpreted as the number of successes in a sequence of $100$ independent experiments.\n\n- Random variable III could *not* be modeled as a binomial distribution. The number of views cannot be interpreted as \"success\" or \"failure.\"\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
