    "q-84050": {
      "dom_id": "step-q84050",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A softball team has a $70%$ chance of winning each game in a $10$-game season. What is the probability that the team wins $9$ of the $10$ games? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of games that the team wins.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=10$ games\n\n- the probability of winning each game is $p=70%=0.7$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(10,0.7).$ We want to find the probability of winning $x=9$ games.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=9) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{10}{9})(0.7)^{9}(1-0.7)^{10-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{10!}{9!(10-9)!}(0.7)^{9}(0.3)^{1} \\\\  & =10(0.7)^{9}(0.3) \\\\  & =0.121\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
