    "q-89366": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89366",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "A spinner with three regions is designed so that the probability it lands on red is $\\frac{3}{10},$ the probability it lands on blue is $\\frac{2}{5},$ and on green $\\frac{3}{10}.$ What is the probability that the spinner lands on red or green exactly $5$ times if it is spun $12$ times? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the spinner lands on red or green.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ spins\n\n- the probability of landing on red or green on any spin is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,\\frac{3}{5}).$ We want to find the probability of $x=5$ successes.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{5}){(\\frac{3}{5})}^{5}{(1-\\frac{3}{5})}^{12-5} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{5!(12-5)!}{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{5}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{7} \\\\  & =792{(\\frac{3}{5})}^{5}{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{7} \\\\  & =0.101\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
