E\"><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>=</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\"><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">(</mo></mrow><mfrac linethickness=\"0\"><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\"><mo minsize=\"2.047em\" maxsize=\"2.047em\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>x</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mn>7</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>We want to find the probability that <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"173\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> or fewer of the <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"174\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c37\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> shots are successful. So, we compute\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax 